<Base title="About — Chef Harris" description="Hi, I'm Harris. I grew up in the Greek countryside, in a family of farmers, and my favourite room in the house was always the kitchen.">
  <h1>Hi, I'm Harris.</h1>

  <p>I grew up in the Greek countryside, in a family of farmers, and my favourite room in the house was always the kitchen. I spent hours there helping my mother and the rest of the family — and experimenting whenever nobody was looking. Later came culinary school, then Switzerland, where I've been a professional chef since.</p>

  <p>For the last four years I've been teaching hobby cooks in person. Not professionals — people who want a Tuesday dinner that tastes like something. What hundreds of them taught me is that the same ten mistakes ruin most meals, and recipes almost never warn you about any of them. Soggy stir-fry, split vinaigrette, onions that never brown. That's what I write about here: what actually happened, and what to do next time.</p>

  <p>Chef Harris, the app, is me in your kitchen when I can't be there — same teaching, same tone.</p>

  <p>Write to me any time: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a></p>
</Base>
